    "research": {
      "notes": "**INOD, news from 2026-09-15 to 2026-10-15**\n\n**1. Guidance / results**\n- No new guidance, pre-announcement or withdrawal found in the window. Yahoo's summary says coverage cites a reaffirmed 40%+ full-year revenue growth outlook, but gives no date for the reaffirmation. It is most likely from the Q2 report — 2026-08-06 (outside the window) — https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/INOD/\n- Q2 (reported 2026-08-06, before the window): revenue was $92.14M against a consensus of $86.31M, up 57.8% year on year — https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/price-innodata-nasdaq-inod-stock-price-down-54-heres-why-2026-10-05/\n- Q2 diluted EPS was $0.41 — 2026-08-06 — https://parameter.io/innodata-inod-stock-surges-15-on-speculation-of-meta-muse-partnership/\n- The next earnings date is estimated at 2026-11-05 — https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/inod/\n\n**2. Analyst actions**\n- BWS Financial maintained its Top Pick rating and $140 target — 2026-09-18 — https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/INOD/\n- TipRanks reports Craig-Hallum reiterated Buy — 2026-09-18 — https://www.cnbc.com/quotes/INOD. No price target was given.\n- MarketBeat says Weiss Ratings and Zacks Research recently downgraded INOD to Hold. Dates are unknown, and the same article gives an average target of $130 — https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/price-innodata-nasdaq-inod-stock-price-down-54-heres-why-2026-10-05/\n- Consensus target is $122.75 (4 analysts, Strong Buy) — 2026-10-14 — https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/inod/\n- The BWS raise to $140 from $110 and Wedbush's raise to $120 from $100 both appear to date from before the window. Wedbush's raise was reported 2026-06-04 — https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/inod/, https://public.com/stocks/inod/news\n\n**3. Litigation / regulation**\n- I found nothing new in the window.\n- Background: the DOJ and SEC closed their probes without enforcement action in a June 2025 8-K. The securities class action over AI statements was still ongoing; a motion to dismiss was filed 2025-03-07 — https://www.tipranks.com/news/company-announcements/innodata-cleared-by-doj-and-sec-in-probes\n- I did not find the current status of the class action.\n- Law-firm \"investigation\" press releases (Bronstein Gewirtz, 2026-03-29) are solicitations, not new proceedings — https://natlawreview.com/press-releases/bronstein-gewirtz-grossman-llc-announces-investigation-against-innodata-2\n\n**4. Customer concentration**\n- Hunterbrook Capital published a report saying Meta is likely Innodata's largest customer and that Muse could be a \"big win.\" Hunterbrook disclosed it was long INOD. Neither company has confirmed the link. The stock rose 14.6% to $69.97 — 2026-09-22 — https://parameter.io/innodata-inod-stock-surges-15-on-speculation-of-meta-muse-partnership/\n- The top customer generated 37% of Q2 revenue, per Motley Fool (Q2 data, reported 2026-08-06) — https://www.fool.com/coverage/better-buy/2026/09/28/innodata-vs-soundhound-ai-which-technology-stock-is-a-better-buy-in-2026/\n- No new customer wins or losses were announced by the company in the window.\n\n**5. Insider activity**\n- Director Louise Forlenza exercised options and sold 10,000 shares at about $55.01 — 2026-09-04 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0000903651/000110465926105529/tm2624878-1_4seq1.xml\n- Forlenza exercised options and sold another 10,000 shares at about $53.54 — 2026-09-14 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0000903651/000110465926107933/tm2625408-2_4seq1.xml\n- Both filings say the sales were for personal financial planning. Neither mentions a 10b5-1 plan.\n- Admiral Michael Rogers joined the board and his Form 3 reports no holdings — 2026-09-15 — https://www.stocktitan.net/overview/INOD/\n- GuruFocus says insiders sold $175.4M over the past 12 months with no buying — 2026-10-12 — https://www.gurufocus.com/news/9120151/innodata-inc-inod-shares-fall-34-what-gf-score-of-84-tells-investors\n- No insider purchases found.\n\n**6. Product / competitive**\n- Innodata opened a New Jersey motion-capture R&D lab, built with Vicon, for humanoid and robot training data and performance validation — 2026-09-30 — https://investor.innodata.com/news/news-details/2026/Innodata-Opens-Motion-Capture-AI-Lab-to-Help-Humanoids-Move-Like-Humans/default.aspx\n- Admiral Michael Rogers (former NSA director and head of US Cyber Command) was appointed to the board, tied to federal and AI strategy — 2026-09-14 (8-K per Stock Titan's listing; TipRanks dates its coverage 2026-09-15) — https://www.stocktitan.net/overview/INOD/\n- Competitive risk: Motley Fool notes Meta holds a big stake in Scale AI and could do more data work in-house — 2026-09-28 — https://www.fool.com/coverage/better-buy/2026/09/28/innodata-vs-soundhound-ai-which-technology-stock-is-a-better-buy-in-2026/\n- I found no pricing news or share-gain data.\n\n**Price context:** INOD closed at $53.14 on 2026-10-14, down 8.98% — https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/inod/. Yahoo reports a smaller regular-session drop of 5.31% for the same day — https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/INOD/. I found no company-specific cause for the drop.",
